  "doc": "The FX kinds (core/render/README.md). One spawn emits `count` particles from a pooled MultiMesh on the `fx` band of the actors canvas. shape is a placeholder analytic sprite in fx_ink.gdshader (disc, streak, burst, splat, bolt) when the FX sheet (`atlas`) is absent; with it, each kind's `atlas` block picks its cells. token: a palette.json id. Particles move on the 60 Hz tick: speed_mps along the spawn angle +- spread_deg/2 (a per-particle hash of the spawn serial, no RNG stream), slowed by drag per second, size grows by grow x per second, fading over the last (1 - fade_from) of life_ticks (fade_from 0 = the whole life). light: a lights.json kind spawned with it (\"\" = none). Budgets: max_particles alive, max_spawns_per_frame; over budget a spawn is dropped and counted. emissive: the kind draws on the fx_emissive band of the emissive canvas, above the lights (FxSystem.glow), with its own budgets. ground: the kind lies on the street (FxSystem.ground on the world canvas's ground_decals band): under the bodies, the shadows and the roofs, and printed by look_d4 like any decal.",
